  "generatedAt": "2026-10-03T02:11:47.574Z",
  "title": "osf review: a base-branch review pipeline with lenses, reviewers and a reducer",
  "summary": "This change adds a whole review subsystem to osf. A new `review.yml` workflow builds osf from the base branch, finds the pull request's work item, runs each configured coding agent as a reviewer in its own job with only its own provider key, and then a final job collects the saved answers, checks every quoted finding against the real files, decides a verdict by fixed rules, and posts it. Supporting this, `osf` gains a lens catalogue (20 shipped lenses plus repository overrides), an agent registry with per-agent read-only and clean-copy switches, a clean copy of the change that strips every agent's project settings, a quote verifier, a reducer with a two-family quorum, a journal payload for answers and decisions, and new `review run`, `review reduce`, `review work-item` and `agents list` commands. The scan suppression engine also learns rule ownership so a marker naming another checker's rule is neither applied nor reported unused.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
